sets.summary:
8 of the 13 planned cells are now proven capturable; 5 are structurally unreachable. Two blockers had to be broken first, and both fixes are proposals, not edits — I changed nothing in the repo.

WHAT THE TWO SURFACES ACTUALLY ARE

O/treasury-modal is BASE DRIFT, not an absent surface. It is the same modal state-specs-5.json already scripts as `O/dev-treasury/*` (SettingsScreen.tsx:1107 TreasuryModal, Developer section). Its dumps have never been produced (dom-dumps has no dev-treasury file), so nothing is lost by adopting the manifest's name — but the two sets must NEVER run together: they are the same picture, and the harness's own distinctness check would reject whichever ran second. State names also drift: manifest `loading` = spec-5 `loading-balances`, `underfunded-rows` = `rows-need-funding`.

O/bundler-funding has exactly ONE render path in the running app. `BundlerFundingView` is a content swap inside SigningRequestModal (SigningRequestModal.tsx:45-50); the standalone `<BundlerFundingModal>` wrapper has NO call site anywhere in src/ (the Send screen shows TreasuryBootstrapSheet instead), and that only call site hard-codes `dappVariant`. Consequence for the plan: the manifest's `topup` and `dapp-variant` are the SAME picture — `topup` as captured already says "Cancel this transaction". `dapp-variant` should be recorded as drift, not drawn.

BLOCKER 1 — no live dApp request, so no sheet. The funding view only exists behind an `eth_sendTransaction`/`wallet_sendCalls` request that has been approved (dapp-connection.tsx:666-698). Fix: the repo's OWN plaintext relay (e2e/support/relay.js — SSE + POST, no crypto) started with a FIXED session and a peer that fires one request on the wallet's SSE rising edge. `deliver()` buffers for a role that is not connected and flushes on connect, so the signing sheet opens by itself right after the connect URL is pasted — zero timing coordination with the capture. Script (proposal, ~50 lines) at /private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-data-production-vela-wallet/8547bccd-7d8f-4d5b-a44a-869806429155/scratchpad/funding-peer.cjs; it registers session `velacapture`/`capnonce`/`capsecret` on port 8788 and fires `eth_sendTransaction {from: fixture one, to: fixture two, value: 0x5af3107a4000, chainId: '0x1'}`. Chain 1 is deliberate: the fixture Safe holds 0 ETH there and is undeployed (latestNonce 0), so nothing this recipe does can land on chain.

BLOCKER 2 — the harness cannot commit a slide-to-confirm. The sheet's single commit control is SlideToConfirmButton, a pointer DRAG (SlideToConfirmButton.tsx:154-200). Its only non-drag path is a `keydown` listener bound to the track ELEMENT (:113-127), which fires only when that element is `document.activeElement`. No act focuses anything, and AppModal cannot supply the focus either: useWebDialog's effect runs while the portal is still unmounted (AppModal.tsx:308-325 sets `mounted` in an EARLIER effect), so `containerRef.current` is null — `role="dialog"` is never set and the Tab trap that would call `first.focus()` never installs. So a synthetic Tab cannot reach into the sheet either. (That is also a small real app bug: AppModal advertises a focus trap it never installs.)

PROPOSED ACT (the whole change — insert before the `clickNth` branch in generator/capture-states.js; full patched copy at .../scratchpad/capture-states-focus.js):

    if (s.act === 'focus') {
      const el = s.id ? document.getElementById(s.id)
        : s.placeholder ? [...document.querySelectorAll('input,textarea')].find((i) => (i.placeholder || '').includes(s.placeholder))
        : s.label ? clickable().find((e) => new RegExp(s.label).test(e.getAttribute('aria-label') || ''))
        : byText(s.text, s.nth);
      if (!el) throw new Error('no element to focus for ' + JSON.stringify(s));
      if (typeof el.focus !== 'function') throw new Error('element is not focusable: ' + JSON.stringify(s));
      el.focus();
      if (document.activeElement !== el) throw new Error('focus() did not take: ' + JSON.stringify(s));
      return sleep(s.ms || 200);
    }

It fails loudly if the element is missing or refuses focus, and it retires an index-fragile step elsewhere too: `focus {placeholder}` + `key Enter` submits the Connections paste field, replacing the `clickNth n:8` that state-specs-4/5 rely on (the same arrow is #2 on /connect and #8 on Home).

DELIVERED SPEC (spec_json): 7 states. Group 1 (treasury, 3 states) runs against TODAY's harness with no preconditions. Group 2 (funding, 4 states) needs the peer process + the focus act, and both requirements are written into the state notes so a run without them fails on a named expectation rather than quietly. Ship group 2 as its own file (state-specs-10.json) if you want group 1 to stay green unconditionally; group 2 must also be ordered LAST in any sweep — it ends with a live dApp session in `vela.remoteInjectSession`, which is exactly what state-specs-5's /connect group declares as a forbidden precondition.

ONE MORE, CAPTURABLE BUT NOT AS A SPEC STATE — O/treasury-modal/unreachable. Its only failure branch is a failed raw `fetchWithTimeout` REST GET (SettingsScreen.tsx:1159-1164); no `vela.*` fault touches it (they all gate poolRpcCall), and the one user-facing lever (Settings > Service Endpoints > VELA RELAY) persists on BLUR, which no act can produce. It IS capturable today through run-capture.mjs's ad-hoc `--pre` path, which evaluates arbitrary JS — proven, exact command in `verified`.
